---
/**
 * The trust page's opening animation, "a kept promise". An AI agent orders from a bakery, directly:
 * the order travels the agent's own line to the bakery's inbox, and the network is not on it. The
 * bakery delivers and its inbox signs a receipt (its seal fills in palm). Then the customer's agent
 * signs that same receipt too: its seal leaves the agent along the agent's own line, comes in at the
 * inbox's door and drops onto the receipt, where the second seal fills in the agent's violet. That
 * receipt, with both seals, and nothing else, travels to the trust network: the message beside it
 * stays in the inbox. The receipt lands on the bakery's listing, the listing's record grows a notch,
 * and the bakery moves up past a salon that has kept fewer promises. Then a coin drops onto the
 * network and falls away, and the order does not move.
 *
 * Why two seals: a record backed only by the business's own word is not ranked. What lifts a
 * business is evidence someone other than the business confirms, starting with the customer's side
 * counter-signing the receipt, so the receipt that travels and the one at rest always carry both.
 *
 * What is drawn is what the page says is live (src/lib/status.ts and the pills under "Today"):
 *  - receipts, live: the inbox signs one, the customer's AI can sign it too, and the network
 *    records it;
 *  - ranking, live: the order reads kept promises, and nobody can pay for a place;
 *  - the record is a gentle meter of notches, as NetworkFlow draws it: no numbers, no stars,
 *    nothing that reads as anyone's real score. The per-listing track record (kept, late or
 *    broken), which the page marks "Being built", is not drawn;
 *  - customers' records are paused, so the agent carries no record of its own here: it signs the
 *    receipt, and that is all it does with it;
 *  - what a network receives is the receipt: no names, no messages, nothing of what was ordered.
 * The order and the agent's signature go from the agent to the business, never through the
 * network. The bakery, the salon and the clinic are illustrations, named by their kind so they can
 * never be a real one.
 *
 * The timings are deliberate and live in GEO.at, where the tests read them; do not retune them by
 * accident.
 *  - One pass and one coda in a 15.45 s loop. The captions change at 0.20, 3.00, 4.40, 6.55,
 *    8.10, 9.55 and 12.25 s, so they hold 2.8, 1.4, 2.15, 1.55, 1.45, 2.7 and 3.4 s (the last one
 *    over the wrap). 1.2 s is the shortest five words can be read in; the six-word counter-sign
 *    phrase gets 2.15. Exactly one phrase is ever on screen: the strip has one text node, and a
 *    new phrase is written only after the old one has faded.
 *  - The beats: the inbox's seal fills at 3.55 s; the agent wakes and its seal travels from 4.45
 *    to 5.85 s and fills the second seal as it lands. The receipt, signed twice, then holds still
 *    under the counter-sign's words for 0.75 s, long enough for the second seal's pop to finish
 *    before anything moves; only then, at 6.6 s, does the receipt set off for the network.
 *    Everything after the counter-sign is the earlier 13.4 s piece moved 2.05 s later, so the rest
 *    of its rhythm is unchanged.
 *  - The directory goes back to where it started at the top of the loop, under the first phrase
 *    and while the eye is on the agent: it fades down, the rows take their old places and the new
 *    notch its old colour, and it fades back. Never under "Nobody can pay for a place", where a
 *    moving order would say the opposite of the words.
 *  - The coin falls with gravity (ease-in), meets the glass at the card's top edge, and falls
 *    away fading. Nothing in the directory moves while it does.
 *  - The piece starts from the picture at rest, 10.95 s into the loop: the order kept, the receipt
 *    docked on the bakery's listing with both seals filled, the new notch, the bakery on top. The
 *    first thing a visitor sees move is the receipt settling into the record. The receipts' route
 *    ends on the bakery's listing and goes where the listing goes, so at rest it points at the
 *    bakery, never at the row the bakery left; at the top of the loop it glides back down while
 *    the rows are faded.
 *
 * Every static part is drawn once below, as a server-rendered SVG built from GEO, in that resting
 * frame. mount() clones it, adds the pieces that move and swaps the clone in whole, so there is
 * never a hole where the figure is: with JavaScript off, or if mount() throws, the picture at rest
 * is what a visitor keeps, and it already shows the whole story. The same GEO reaches the script
 * as JSON on the figure, so the drawing and the machine cannot disagree about where anything is.
 * The figure holds aspect-ratio 520/390 from first paint, so nothing below it jumps. With reduced
 * motion the machine renders that same frame and stops; the preference is honoured if it is
 * turned on later. Off-screen or in a hidden tab the clock stops.
 *
 * The styles are global because the moving pieces are made at run time, where Astro's scoped
 * selectors cannot reach. Nothing leaks: every selector begins with .stf, every keyframe is named
 * stf-*, and the tf- class names exist only inside .stf. None of them overlap HeroFlow's .sdf,
 * NetworkFlow's .snf or HowFlow's .shf.
 *
 * Colours are the site's tokens, with a literal fallback only for a host that has not declared
 * them; night redefines the fallbacks under both the prefers-color-scheme query and
 * [data-theme="dark"]. No red anywhere: ink, the order's tangerine, the palm of a kept promise,
 * the agent's violet and a coin's sun gold, and no pink outside the brand's own mark, which keeps
 * the brand's own gradient as Mark.astro draws it. The order's word is drawn in its ink pulled toward
 * --ink (18% by day, 32% by night), as NetworkFlow does, so it clears 4.5:1 and keeps its hue.
 *
 * No max-width of its own: the piece is whatever its container is (the page's .art-box caps it).
 */

/** The world, in the 520x390 viewBox. The drawing below and the script both read this. */
const GEO = {
  agent: { x: 30, y: 134 },
  /** the agent to the business's inbox, directly: the network is not on this line */
  ask: "M56,134 C80,134 72,160 96,160",
  /** the route receipts take, from the inbox's door to the network's. The far end is the door on
      the bakery's listing, so it goes where the listing goes: it is drawn to the listing's centre. */
  link: { x0: 240, y0: 160, bend: 268, x1: 296 },
  /** the receipt's whole journey: off the order's row, along the link, onto the listing, which is
      still in its first place while the receipt travels */
  road: "M236,160 L240,160 C268,160 268,192 296,192 L305,192",
  /** the customer's signature: out of the agent along its own line to the inbox's door, then in
      the groove above the order and down onto the receipt, to the seal the agent signs. It never
      leaves the agent's line and the inbox, so the network is not on it either. */
  sign: "M56,134 C80,134 72,160 96,160 C102,160 102,142 112,142 L223,142 C230,142 232.6,154 232.6,164.6",
  /** the receipt's two seals, from its centre: the inbox's on the right, the agent's on the left,
      with a clear gap between them so they read as two even at a phone's width */
  seals: { ib: [3.4, 4.6], ag: [-3.4, 4.6], r: 2.5 },
  ports: [
    [96, 160],
    [240, 160],
  ],
  inbox: { x: 96, y: 102, w: 144, h: 126, name: "Bakery", room: 96 },
  item: { x: 104, y: 146, w: 128, h: 28, lb: "Order", st: "Delivered" },
  /** what stays in the inbox: the message, the name, what was ordered */
  msg: { x: 104, y: 184, w: 128, h: 30 },
  net: { x: 296, y: 102, w: 208, h: 152, name: "Trust network" },
  row: { x: 308, w: 184, h: 28, slots: [146, 178, 210], notchX: 14, notchStep: 5.4, notches: 5, nameX: 52 },
  /** in the order they start in; the pass row overtakes the one above it */
  rows: [
    { name: "Salon", level: 3 },
    { name: "Bakery", level: 3 },
    { name: "Clinic", level: 2 },
  ],
  pass: { r: 1, over: 0 },
  /** the receipt docks on its listing's left edge, beside the meter */
  dockX: 305,
  coin: { x: 452, from: 20, edge: 102, r: 7 },
  say: {
    cx: 260,
    y: 302,
    h: 20,
    w: 200,
    phrases: [
      "A business keeps its promise",
      "Its inbox signs a receipt",
      "The customer's AI signs it too",
      "Just the receipt travels",
      "Its record grows a notch",
      "The order follows kept promises",
      "Nobody can pay for a place",
    ],
  },
  /** the timeline, in seconds into the loop */
  at: {
    loop: 15.45,
    rest: 10.95,
    say: [0.2, 3.0, 4.4, 6.55, 8.1, 9.55, 12.25],
    reset: [0.2, 1.2],
    ask: [0.35, 1.3],
    item: 1.5,
    kept: 2.4,
    slip: 3.05,
    seal: 3.55,
    sign: [4.45, 5.85],
    road: [6.6, 7.9],
    notch: 8.1,
    swap: [9.6, 10.5],
    settle: [11.55, 11.95],
    coin: [12.35, 13.05, 13.95],
  },
};

const { agent, inbox, item, msg, net, row, say, seals } = GEO;
/* At rest the pass row has overtaken: it holds the slot above, and the one it passed holds its. */
const slotAtRest = GEO.rows.map((_, i) => (i === GEO.pass.r ? GEO.pass.over : i === GEO.pass.over ? GEO.pass.r : i));
const passY = row.slots[slotAtRest[GEO.pass.r] ?? 0] ?? 0;
/* the receipts' route, to a door at height y; at rest that door is on the bakery, in its new place */
const L = GEO.link;
const linkTo = (y: number) => `M${L.x0},${L.y0} C${L.bend},${L.y0} ${L.bend},${y} ${L.x1},${y}`;
const door = passY + row.h / 2;
/* the inbox's mark: the striped half sun, as on the other pages' business cards */
const sunY = inbox.y + 25;
const sun = `M${inbox.x + 12},${sunY} A7,7 0 0 1 ${inbox.x + 26},${sunY} Z`;
/* the network's mark: three listings, linked, sitting on the title's baseline */
const glyph = [
  [net.x + 14.5, net.y + 24.5],
  [net.x + 22, net.y + 13.5],
  [net.x + 29.5, net.y + 24.5],
];
/* A rough width for the picture at rest; the script measures the real one. */
const est = (s: string, fs: number) => Math.round(s.length * fs * 0.54);
const sayW = Math.max(say.w, ...say.phrases.map((p) => est(p, 9) + 34));
const sayX = say.cx - sayW / 2;
/* Below the breakpoint the phrase is drawn larger (the container query below), so the picture at
   rest also carries a phone's strip, shown only there; the script drops it and measures its own.
   The phrase's x is say.cx + 5 at either width. */
const sayWn = Math.max(say.w, ...say.phrases.map((p) => est(p, 12.4) + 34));
const sayXn = say.cx - sayWn / 2;
/* the phrase on screen at rest */
const restSay = GEO.at.say.filter((t) => t <= GEO.at.rest).length - 1;
---

<figure class="stf" aria-label="How a kept promise orders the directory" data-tf={JSON.stringify(GEO)}>
  <svg class="tf-seed" viewBox="0 0 520 390" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <defs>
      <!-- the brand's mark, in the brand's own gradient, as Mark.astro draws it -->
      <linearGradient id="tfseed-g" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--tangerine, #ff9650)"></stop>
        <stop offset="58%" stop-color="var(--flamingo, #ff6fa8)"></stop>
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--violet, #8a6bff)"></stop>
      </linearGradient>
      <clipPath id="tfseed-c"><path d={sun}></path></clipPath>
    </defs>

    <g class="tf-lines">
      <path d={GEO.ask} class="tf-line" />
      <path d={linkTo(door)} class="tf-line tf-link" />
    </g>

    <text x={agent.x} y="90" font-size="8.2" class="tf-cap">AI AGENT</text>
    <g class="tf-agent">
      <rect x={agent.x} y={agent.y - 12} width="24" height="24" rx="7" class="bodyfill" />
      <rect x={agent.x} y={agent.y - 12} width="24" height="24" rx="7" />
      <rect x={agent.x - 4} y={agent.y - 16} width="32" height="32" rx="10" class="halo" />
      <circle cx={agent.x + 7.6} cy={agent.y - 1} r="1.7" class="eye" />
      <circle cx={agent.x + 16.4} cy={agent.y - 1} r="1.7" class="eye" />
      <line x1={agent.x + 12} y1={agent.y - 12} x2={agent.x + 12} y2={agent.y - 19} />
      <circle cx={agent.x + 12} cy={agent.y - 21.6} r="2.6" class="ant" />
    </g>

    <g class="tf-ib">
      <rect x={inbox.x} y={inbox.y} width={inbox.w} height={inbox.h} rx="14" class="tf-glass" />
      <g class="tf-sun">
        <path d={sun} fill="url(#tfseed-g)"></path>
        <g clip-path="url(#tfseed-c)">
          {[5.5, 4, 2.7].map((d) => (
            <rect x={inbox.x + 11} y={sunY - d} width="16" height=".6" fill="var(--tf-ground)" />
          ))}
        </g>
      </g>
      <text x={inbox.x + 34} y={sunY} font-size="12" class="tf-title tf-ibname">{inbox.name}</text>
      <line x1={inbox.x + 12} y1={inbox.y + 36} x2={inbox.x + inbox.w - 12} y2={inbox.y + 36} class="tf-hair" />
      <g class="tf-item on res" transform={`translate(${item.x},${item.y})`}>
        <rect width={item.w} height={item.h} rx="8" class="bg" />
        <rect y="5" width="2.5" height={item.h - 10} rx="1.25" class="bar" />
        <text x="10" y="17.8" font-size="9.6" class="lb">{item.lb}</text>
        <g class="res">
          <text x={item.w - 24} y="17.8" font-size="8.4" text-anchor="end" class="st">{item.st}</text>
          <path d={`M${item.w - 18.6},14.4 l2.7,2.9 l5.1,-6.2`} class="tf-tick" />
        </g>
      </g>
      <g class="tf-msg" transform={`translate(${msg.x},${msg.y})`}>
        <rect width={msg.w} height={msg.h} rx="8" class="bg" />
        <path d="M10.5,9.5 h11 a2.5,2.5 0 0 1 2.5,2.5 v4 a2.5,2.5 0 0 1 -2.5,2.5 h-6 l-3,2.6 v-2.6 h-2 a2.5,2.5 0 0 1 -2.5,-2.5 v-4 a2.5,2.5 0 0 1 2.5,-2.5 Z" class="ic" />
        <rect x="32" y="10.2" width="74" height="2.6" rx="1.3" class="ln" />
        <rect x="32" y="17.2" width="48" height="2.6" rx="1.3" class="ln" />
      </g>
    </g>

    <g class="tf-net">
      <rect x={net.x} y={net.y} width={net.w} height={net.h} rx="14" class="tf-glass" />
      <g class="tf-glyph">
        <path d={`M${glyph.map(([x, y]) => `${x},${y}`).join(" L")} Z`} />
        {glyph.map(([x, y]) => <circle cx={x} cy={y} r="2.3" />)}
      </g>
      <text x={net.x + 38} y={net.y + 25} font-size="12" class="tf-title">{net.name}</text>
      <line x1={net.x + 12} y1={net.y + 36} x2={net.x + net.w - 12} y2={net.y + 36} class="tf-hair" />
      <g class="tf-dirs">
        {
          GEO.rows.map((r, i) => {
            const gained = i === GEO.pass.r;
            return (
              <g
                class={gained ? "tf-dir hit" : "tf-dir"}
                transform={`translate(${row.x},${row.slots[slotAtRest[i] ?? i] ?? 0})`}
              >
                <rect width={row.w} height={row.h} rx="8" class="bg" />
                <rect width={row.w} height={row.h} rx="8" class="ring" />
                {Array.from({ length: row.notches }, (_, k) => (
                  <rect
                    x={row.notchX + k * row.notchStep}
                    y="9"
                    width="3.2"
                    height="10"
                    rx="1.4"
                    class={k < r.level ? "tf-notch on" : gained && k === r.level ? "tf-notch on new" : "tf-notch"}
                  />
                ))}
                <text x={row.nameX} y="17.8" font-size="9.2" class="nm">{r.name}</text>
              </g>
            );
          })
        }
      </g>
    </g>

    {GEO.ports.map(([x, y]) => <circle cx={x} cy={y} r="2.6" class="tf-port" />)}
    <circle cx={L.x1} cy={door} r="2.6" class="tf-port tf-door" />

    <!-- at rest the receipt carries both seals: the inbox's, and the customer's agent's -->
    <g class="tf-slip signed cosigned" transform={`translate(${GEO.dockX},${passY + row.h / 2})`}>
      <rect x="-7" y="-9" width="14" height="18" rx="2.3" class="paper" />
      <line x1="-3.6" y1="-4.9" x2="3.6" y2="-4.9" class="ln" />
      <line x1="-3.6" y1="-1.9" x2="1.8" y2="-1.9" class="ln" />
      <circle cx={seals.ib[0]} cy={seals.ib[1]} r={seals.r} class="seal ib" />
      <circle cx={seals.ag[0]} cy={seals.ag[1]} r={seals.r} class="seal ag" />
    </g>

    <g class="tf-say">
      <rect x={sayX} y={say.y} width={sayW} height={say.h} rx={say.h / 2} class="tf-wide" />
      <circle cx={sayX + 12} cy={say.y + say.h / 2} r="3" class="tf-beat tf-wide" />
      <rect x={sayXn} y={say.y} width={sayWn} height={say.h} rx={say.h / 2} class="tf-narrow" />
      <circle cx={sayXn + 12} cy={say.y + say.h / 2} r="3" class="tf-beat tf-narrow" />
      <text x={sayX + (sayW + 10) / 2} y={say.y + 13.2} font-size="9" text-anchor="middle" class="tf-phrase on">{say.phrases[restSay]}</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="tf-sr">
    An AI agent orders bread from a bakery, directly. The bakery delivers, and its inbox signs a receipt. The
    customer's agent signs the same receipt too, on its own line to the bakery. Just the receipt, carrying both
    signatures, goes to the trust network, with no names, no messages and nothing of what was ordered. The bakery's
    record grows a notch, and it moves up past a salon that has kept fewer promises. A coin dropped on the network falls
    away, and the order does not move: nobody can pay for a place. The businesses are illustrations.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style is:global>
  /* Every selector below begins with .stf and every keyframe is named stf-*. */
  .stf {
    --tf-ground: var(--ground, #f6f5ff);
    --tf-ink: var(--ink, #14163c);
    --tf-ink2: var(--ink-2, #474a75);
    --tf-ink3: var(--ink-3, #6b6e96);
    --tf-hair: var(--hairline, rgba(20, 22, 60, 0.08));
    --tf-glass: var(--glass-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.32));
    --tf-glassb: var(--glass-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55));
    --tf-row: var(--row-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.24));
    --tf-order: var(--c-order, #ff9650);
    --tf-order-i: var(--c-order-ink, #9c4409);
    --tf-palm: var(--c-success, #2fd3a5);
    --tf-palm-i: var(--c-success-ink, #147a5c);
    --tf-violet: var(--violet, #8a6bff);
    --tf-sun: var(--sun, #ffcf5c);
    --tf-sun-i: var(--sun-ink, #866000);
    --tf-ease: var(--ease-out-soft, cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1));
    /* how much of the order's ink is kept when its word is pulled toward --ink */
    --tf-tmix: 82%;
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    margin: 0;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 520 / 390;
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .stf {
      --tf-ground: var(--ground, #0d0e26);
      --tf-ink: var(--ink, #f2f1ff);
      --tf-ink2: var(--ink-2, #b9b8dd);
      --tf-ink3: var(--ink-3, #8e8db8);
      --tf-hair: var(--hairline, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
      --tf-glass: var(--glass-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07));
      --tf-glassb: var(--glass-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14));
      --tf-row: var(--row-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
      --tf-order-i: var(--c-order-ink, #ffb27c);
      --tf-palm-i: var(--c-success-ink, #72e6c3);
      --tf-sun-i: var(--sun-ink, #ffda80);
      --tf-tmix: 68%;
    }
  }
  [data-theme="dark"] .stf {
    --tf-ground: var(--ground, #0d0e26);
    --tf-ink: var(--ink, #f2f1ff);
    --tf-ink2: var(--ink-2, #b9b8dd);
    --tf-ink3: var(--ink-3, #8e8db8);
    --tf-hair: var(--hairline, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
    --tf-glass: var(--glass-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07));
    --tf-glassb: var(--glass-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14));
    --tf-row: var(--row-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
    --tf-order-i: var(--c-order-ink, #ffb27c);
    --tf-palm-i: var(--c-success-ink, #72e6c3);
    --tf-sun-i: var(--sun-ink, #ffda80);
    --tf-tmix: 68%;
  }

  .stf svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .stf text {
    font-family: var(--font-sans, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif);
    fill: var(--tf-ink2);
  }
  .stf .tf-cap {
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
  }
  .stf .tf-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  /* thin lines: the agent's own line to the business, and the receipts' route */
  .stf .tf-line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-opacity: 0.34;
    stroke-width: 1.1;
  }
  .stf .tf-port {
    fill: var(--tf-ink3);
    fill-opacity: 0.55;
  }

  /* glass: a wash and a hairline, never a shadow */
  .stf .tf-glass {
    fill: var(--tf-glass);
    stroke: var(--tf-glassb);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .stf .tf-hair {
    stroke: var(--tf-hair);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .stf .tf-glyph path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-opacity: 0.5;
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .stf .tf-glyph circle {
    fill: var(--tf-ink3);
  }

  /* the agent: drawn in ink, its identity in one small tinted dot */
  .stf .tf-agent rect,
  .stf .tf-agent line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-ink2);
    stroke-opacity: 0.55;
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }
  .stf .tf-agent .bodyfill {
    fill: var(--tf-violet);
    fill-opacity: 0.07;
    stroke: none;
  }
  .stf .tf-agent .eye {
    fill: var(--tf-ink2);
    fill-opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .stf .tf-agent .ant {
    fill: var(--tf-violet);
  }
  .stf .tf-agent .halo {
    stroke: var(--tf-violet);
    stroke-opacity: 0;
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  }
  .stf .tf-agent.wake .halo {
    animation: stf-halo 0.62s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  @keyframes stf-halo {
    0% {
      stroke-opacity: 0.55;
      transform: scale(0.82);
    }
    100% {
      stroke-opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(1.3);
    }
  }

  /* the order, in the business's inbox */
  .stf .tf-item {
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.3s linear;
  }
  .stf .tf-item.on {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .stf .tf-item .bg {
    fill: var(--tf-row);
  }
  .stf .tf-item .bar {
    fill: var(--tf-order);
  }
  .stf .tf-item .lb {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tf-order-i) var(--tf-tmix), var(--tf-ink));
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .stf .tf-item .res {
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.36s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  .stf .tf-item.res .res {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .stf .tf-tick {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-palm-i);
    stroke-width: 1.7;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  /* what stays in the inbox */
  .stf .tf-msg .bg {
    fill: var(--tf-row);
  }
  .stf .tf-msg .ic {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-opacity: 0.55;
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .stf .tf-msg .ln {
    fill: var(--tf-ink3);
    fill-opacity: 0.3;
    transition: fill-opacity 0.5s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  .stf .tf-msg.stay .ln {
    fill-opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* the directory */
  .stf .tf-dir .bg {
    fill: var(--tf-row);
    stroke: var(--tf-palm);
    stroke-opacity: 0;
    stroke-width: 1;
    transition: stroke-opacity 0.36s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  .stf .tf-dir.hit .bg {
    stroke-opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .stf .tf-dir .ring {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-palm);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
    opacity: 0;
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  }
  .stf .tf-dir.ping .ring {
    animation: stf-ping 0.72s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  @keyframes stf-ping {
    0% {
      opacity: 0.5;
      transform: scale(1);
    }
    100% {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(1.06, 1.3);
    }
  }
  .stf .tf-dir .nm {
    fill: var(--tf-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* The record: a few notches, never a number. A notch that has just been
     earned comes in palm and grows up out of its slot. */
  .stf .tf-notch {
    fill: var(--tf-ink3);
    fill-opacity: 0.2;
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: 50% 100%;
    transition:
      fill 1s var(--tf-ease),
      fill-opacity 1s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  .stf .tf-notch.on {
    fill-opacity: 0.62;
  }
  .stf .tf-notch.new {
    fill: var(--tf-palm);
    fill-opacity: 1;
    transition: none;
  }
  /* the moves are their own classes, added only as they happen, so the
     picture at rest never plays them on arrival */
  .stf .tf-notch.grow {
    animation: stf-grow 0.7s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  @keyframes stf-grow {
    0% {
      transform: scaleY(0.2);
    }
    60% {
      transform: scaleY(1.18);
    }
    100% {
      transform: scaleY(1);
    }
  }

  /* the receipt: paper, two lines, and two seals, each a dashed ring until its side signs: the
     inbox's in palm, then the customer's agent's in the agent's violet */
  .stf .tf-slip .paper {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tf-palm) 10%, var(--tf-ground));
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-opacity: 0.6;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .stf .tf-slip .ln {
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-opacity: 0.7;
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .stf .tf-slip .seal {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-opacity: 0.5;
    stroke-width: 0.9;
    stroke-dasharray: 1.4 1.2;
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  }
  .stf .tf-slip.signed .seal.ib {
    fill: var(--tf-palm);
    stroke: none;
  }
  .stf .tf-slip.cosigned .seal.ag {
    fill: var(--tf-violet);
    stroke: none;
  }
  .stf .tf-slip.pop .seal.ib,
  .stf .tf-slip.copop .seal.ag {
    animation: stf-pop 0.6s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  @keyframes stf-pop {
    0% {
      transform: scale(0.4);
    }
    55% {
      transform: scale(1.6);
    }
    100% {
      transform: scale(1);
    }
  }

  /* the pieces that move */
  /* the order on its way, in the order's tangerine: on the agent's line, violet is only ever the
     customer's AI's signature */
  .stf .tf-dot {
    fill: var(--tf-order);
  }
  /* the agent's seal on its way to the receipt: the seal itself, in a faint ring */
  .stf .tf-ink .core {
    fill: var(--tf-violet);
  }
  .stf .tf-ink .rim {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-violet);
    stroke-opacity: 0.35;
    stroke-width: 0.8;
  }
  .stf .tf-coin .face {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tf-sun) 55%, var(--tf-ground));
    stroke: var(--tf-sun-i);
    stroke-opacity: 0.7;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .stf .tf-coin .rim {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-sun-i);
    stroke-opacity: 0.55;
    stroke-width: 0.9;
  }
  .stf .tf-coin .edge {
    fill: var(--tf-sun-i);
    fill-opacity: 0.4;
  }
  .stf .tf-ripple {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-width: 1;
    opacity: 0;
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  }
  .stf .tf-ripple.hit {
    animation: stf-ripple 0.8s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  @keyframes stf-ripple {
    0% {
      opacity: 0.6;
      transform: scale(0.5);
    }
    100% {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(1.6);
    }
  }
  .stf .tf-off {
    display: none;
  }
  .stf .tf-guide {
    fill: none;
    stroke: none;
  }

  /* the caption strip: one phrase, faded out before the next is written */
  .stf .tf-say rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--tf-ink3);
    stroke-opacity: 0.3;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .stf .tf-beat {
    fill: var(--tf-palm);
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  }
  .stf .tf-say.beat .tf-beat {
    animation: stf-beat 0.7s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  @keyframes stf-beat {
    0% {
      transform: scale(1);
    }
    36% {
      transform: scale(1.5);
    }
    100% {
      transform: scale(1);
    }
  }
  .stf .tf-phrase {
    fill: var(--tf-ink2);
    font-weight: 500;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.16s linear;
  }
  .stf .tf-phrase.on {
    opacity: 1;
    transition: opacity 0.24s var(--tf-ease);
  }
  /* the phone's strip, drawn only in the picture at rest and only below the breakpoint */
  .stf .tf-narrow {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Read by a screen reader, not drawn. */
  .stf .tf-sr {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: -1px;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* Below the breakpoint the viewBox shrinks the type past reading size, so the
     words that carry the story grow in user units: the caption, the card
     titles, the names, the order's word and the phrase. Targets are CSS pixels
     at a 342-wide art-box (a 390px phone) divided by the container scale. The
     order's status steps out because it cannot grow inside its row; the tick
     still says it was delivered. The script measures the phrases again after
     the switch, so a bigger word gets a bigger strip; without the script, the
     picture at rest swaps to the wider strip it carries for this. */
  @container (max-width: 460px) {
    .stf .tf-item .st {
      display: none;
    }
    .stf .tf-cap {
      font-size: 12.4px;
    }
    .stf .tf-title {
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .stf .tf-dir .nm {
      font-size: 12.6px;
    }
    .stf .tf-item .lb {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .stf .tf-phrase {
      font-size: 12.4px;
    }
    .stf .tf-seed .tf-narrow {
      display: inline;
    }
    .stf .tf-seed .tf-wide {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* Reduced motion: the machine renders the picture at rest and stops, and
     every transition and keyframe inside the figure is switched off. Paused,
     the CSS keyframes stop with the clock. */
  .stf.tf-still *,
  .stf.tf-still {
    animation: none !important;
    transition: none !important;
  }
  .stf.tf-paused * {
    animation-play-state: paused !important;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .stf * {
      animation: none !important;
      transition: none !important;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  /* The drawing machine. It clones the server-rendered picture, adds the pieces
     that move, and draws every frame from the time alone, so any moment of the
     loop can be drawn without playing the ones before it. */
  type Geo = {
    agent: { x: number; y: number };
    ask: string;
    link: { x0: number; y0: number; bend: number; x1: number };
    road: string;
    sign: string;
    seals: { ib: number[]; ag: number[]; r: number };
    item: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number };
    inbox: { room: number };
    row: { x: number; h: number; slots: number[]; notchX: number; notchStep: number };
    rows: { name: string; level: number }[];
    pass: { r: number; over: number };
    dockX: number;
    coin: { x: number; from: number; edge: number; r: number };
    say: { cx: number; w: number; phrases: string[] };
    at: {
      loop: number;
      rest: number;
      say: number[];
      reset: [number, number];
      ask: [number, number];
      item: number;
      kept: number;
      slip: number;
      seal: number;
      sign: [number, number];
      road: [number, number];
      notch: number;
      swap: [number, number];
      settle: [number, number];
      coin: [number, number, number];
    };
  };

  const NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
  function E<K extends keyof SVGElementTagNameMap>(n: K, a: Record<string, string | number> = {}): SVGElementTagNameMap[K] {
    const e = document.createElementNS(NS, n);
    for (const k in a) e.setAttribute(k, String(a[k]));
    return e;
  }
  function all<T extends Element>(root: ParentNode, sel: string): T[] {
    return Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<T>(sel));
  }
  function one<T extends Element>(root: ParentNode, sel: string): T {
    const e = root.querySelector<T>(sel);
    if (!e) throw new Error(`trust flow: missing ${sel}`);
    return e;
  }
  function must<T>(v: T | undefined, what: string): T {
    if (v === undefined) throw new Error(`trust flow: missing ${what}`);
    return v;
  }

  /* Newton solve for a CSS cubic-bezier, so the travel uses the same curve as
     the CSS transitions around it. */
  function bez(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number) {
    const cx = 3 * x1;
    const bx = 3 * (x2 - x1) - cx;
    const ax = 1 - cx - bx;
    const cy = 3 * y1;
    const by = 3 * (y2 - y1) - cy;
    const ay = 1 - cy - by;
    return (x: number) => {
      let t = x;
      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        const e = ((ax * t + bx) * t + cx) * t - x;
        if (Math.abs(e) < 1e-4) break;
        const d = (3 * ax * t + 2 * bx) * t + cx;
        if (Math.abs(d) < 1e-6) break;
        t -= e / d;
      }
      return ((ay * t + by) * t + cy) * t;
    };
  }
  const eSoft = bez(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
  const eSine = (t: number) => -(Math.cos(Math.PI * t) - 1) / 2;
  const cl = (v: number) => (v < 0 ? 0 : v > 1 ? 1 : v);
  const lerp = (a: number, b: number, u: number) => a + (b - a) * u;
  const within = (t: number, [a, b]: readonly number[]) => t >= (a ?? 0) && t < (b ?? 0);
  const prog = (t: number, a: number, b: number) => cl((t - a) / (b - a));

  let seq = 0;

  function mount(fig: HTMLElement) {
    if (fig.dataset.tfOn === "on") return; /* one scene per figure, however often this runs */
    fig.dataset.tfOn = "on";
    const G = JSON.parse(fig.dataset.tf ?? "") as Geo;
    const A = G.at;
    const seed = one<SVGSVGElement>(fig, "svg.tf-seed");

    /* The live scene is the picture at rest plus the pieces that move. It is
       built off the page and swapped in whole, so the figure is never empty. */
    const svg = seed.cloneNode(true) as SVGSVGElement;
    svg.classList.remove("tf-seed");
    /* the phone's strip is the seed's alone: the live strip is measured (fit, below) */
    for (const el of all(svg, ".tf-narrow")) el.remove();
    const uid = `tf${++seq}`;
    one(svg, "#tfseed-g").id = `${uid}g`;
    one(svg, "#tfseed-c").id = `${uid}c`;
    for (const el of all(svg, '[fill="url(#tfseed-g)"]')) el.setAttribute("fill", `url(#${uid}g)`);
    for (const el of all(svg, '[clip-path="url(#tfseed-c)"]')) el.setAttribute("clip-path", `url(#${uid}c)`);

    const agent = one<SVGGElement>(svg, ".tf-agent");
    const itemG = one<SVGGElement>(svg, ".tf-item");
    const msgG = one<SVGGElement>(svg, ".tf-msg");
    const dirsG = one<SVGGElement>(svg, ".tf-dirs");
    const dirs = all<SVGGElement>(dirsG, ".tf-dir");
    const pass = must(dirs[G.pass.r], "the listing that moves up");
    const gain = must(all<SVGRectElement>(pass, ".tf-notch")[G.rows[G.pass.r]?.level ?? 0], "the notch it earns");
    const slip = one<SVGGElement>(svg, ".tf-slip");
    const ibName = one<SVGTextElement>(svg, ".tf-ibname");
    const sayG = one<SVGGElement>(svg, ".tf-say");
    const sayRect = one<SVGRectElement>(sayG, "rect");
    const sayDot = one<SVGCircleElement>(sayG, ".tf-beat");
    const phrase = one<SVGTextElement>(sayG, ".tf-phrase");
    const linkEl = one<SVGPathElement>(svg, ".tf-link");
    const doorEl = one<SVGCircleElement>(svg, ".tf-door");

    /* the pieces made here: the order's dot, the agent's seal on its way, the coin and the glass's
       answer to it */
    const dot = E("circle", { r: 3.2, class: "tf-dot tf-off" });
    const ink = E("g", { class: "tf-ink tf-off" });
    ink.append(E("circle", { r: G.seals.r + 0.4, class: "rim" }), E("circle", { r: G.seals.r, class: "core" }));
    const coin = E("g", { class: "tf-coin tf-off" });
    const C = G.coin;
    coin.append(
      E("ellipse", { cy: 1.6, rx: C.r, ry: C.r, class: "edge" }),
      E("circle", { r: C.r, class: "face" }),
      E("circle", { r: C.r - 2.6, class: "rim" }),
    );
    const ripple = E("ellipse", { cx: C.x, cy: C.edge, rx: 14, ry: 3.2, class: "tf-ripple" });
    svg.append(dot, ink, ripple, coin);
    /* unpainted guides the moving pieces follow */
    const askPath = E("path", { d: G.ask, class: "tf-guide" });
    const signPath = E("path", { d: G.sign, class: "tf-guide" });
    const roadPath = E("path", { d: G.road, class: "tf-guide" });
    svg.append(askPath, signPath, roadPath);

    /* Anything that throws from here on leaves a drawn scene, not a hole. */
    seed.replaceWith(svg);

    const LASK = askPath.getTotalLength();
    const LSIGN = signPath.getTotalLength();
    const LROAD = roadPath.getTotalLength();
    const birth = roadPath.getPointAtLength(0);

    /* ---- words are measured, never guessed ------------------------------ */
    function bx(t: SVGGraphicsElement): DOMRect | null {
      try {
        const b = t.getBBox();
        return b?.width ? b : null;
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
    }
    function fit() {
      /* the caption strip holds its widest phrase, so it never changes size under a phrase */
      const said = phrase.textContent;
      let widest = 0;
      for (const p of G.say.phrases) {
        phrase.textContent = p;
        widest = Math.max(widest, bx(phrase)?.width ?? 0);
      }
      phrase.textContent = said;
      const W = Math.max(G.say.w, Math.ceil(widest + 34));
      const x0 = G.say.cx - W / 2;
      sayRect.setAttribute("x", String(x0));
      sayRect.setAttribute("width", String(W));
      sayDot.setAttribute("cx", String(x0 + 12));
      phrase.setAttribute("x", String(x0 + (W + 10) / 2));
      /* the inbox's title shrinks only if a wide fallback font would push it out of its card */
      ibName.style.fontSize = "";
      const b = bx(ibName);
      if (b && b.width > G.inbox.room) {
        const px = Number.parseFloat(getComputedStyle(ibName).fontSize) || 12;
        ibName.style.fontSize = `${((px * G.inbox.room) / b.width).toFixed(2)}px`;
      }
    }
    /* The type scale changes at the container breakpoint, so the words are
       re-measured when the piece crosses it, when a hidden piece is first
       revealed, and once more when the webfonts have arrived. */
    let narrow: boolean | null = null;
    let measured = false;
    function gauge() {
      const w = fig.clientWidth;
      const nw = w > 0 && w <= 460;
      if (nw === narrow && measured) return;
      narrow = nw;
      if (w > 0) {
        fit();
        measured = true;
      }
    }
    gauge();
    if ("ResizeObserver" in window) new ResizeObserver(gauge).observe(fig);
    document.fonts?.ready.then(fit, () => {});

    /* ---- the pieces ------------------------------------------------------ */
    function put(el: SVGElement, x: number, y: number, s = 1) {
      el.setAttribute("transform", `translate(${x},${y})${s === 1 ? "" : ` scale(${s})`}`);
      el.classList.remove("tf-off");
    }
    function off(el: SVGElement) {
      el.classList.add("tf-off");
    }
    /* Highlights are wall-clock, so every timer is held here: a paused or
       stilled piece must not have a late timer reach in and undo it. */
    const timers: number[] = [];
    function hold(ms: number, fn: () => void) {
      timers.push(window.setTimeout(fn, ms));
    }
    function flash(el: Element, cls: string, ms: number) {
      el.classList.remove(cls);
      void el.getBoundingClientRect(); /* a reflow, so a repeated highlight starts again */
      el.classList.add(cls);
      hold(ms, () => el.classList.remove(cls));
    }

    /* One phrase on screen at a time: a single text node, faded out before the
       next phrase is written into it. */
    let want = phrase.textContent?.trim() ?? "";
    function sayIt(i: number, live: boolean) {
      const text = G.say.phrases[i] ?? "";
      if (text === want) return;
      want = text;
      if (!live) {
        phrase.textContent = text;
        phrase.classList.add("on");
        return;
      }
      phrase.classList.remove("on");
      flash(sayG, "beat", 720);
      hold(170, () => {
        phrase.textContent = want;
        phrase.classList.add("on");
      });
    }

    /* ---- one moment of the loop ----------------------------------------- */
    const slotY = (slot: number) => G.row.slots[slot] ?? 0;
    const restY = (i: number) => slotY(i);
    const endY = (i: number) => slotY(i === G.pass.r ? G.pass.over : i === G.pass.over ? G.pass.r : i);
    const mid = ((A.reset[0] ?? 0) + (A.reset[1] ?? 0)) / 2;
    const half = G.row.h / 2;
    const level = G.rows[G.pass.r]?.level ?? 0;
    const notchX = G.row.x + G.row.notchX + level * G.row.notchStep + 1.6;
    /* a mark is crossed when the clock passes it between two frames, wrap included */
    const crossed = (a: number, b: number, m: number) => (b >= a ? a < m && m <= b : m > a || m <= b);
    const L = G.link;
    const linkTo = (y: number) => `M${L.x0},${L.y0} C${L.bend},${L.y0} ${L.bend},${y} ${L.x1},${y}`;
    let doorAt = Number.NaN;

    function render(t: number, prev: number, live: boolean) {
      /* the caption: the last phrase whose time has come, the coda's before the first */
      let s = G.say.phrases.length - 1;
      A.say.forEach((at, i) => {
        if (t >= at) s = i;
      });
      sayIt(s, live);

      /* 1. the agent orders from the business itself, on its own line */
      if (live && crossed(prev, t, A.ask[0])) flash(agent, "wake", 640);
      if (within(t, A.ask)) {
        const v = prog(t, A.ask[0], A.ask[1]);
        const p = askPath.getPointAtLength(eSine(v) * LASK);
        dot.style.opacity = String(v < 0.15 ? v / 0.15 : 1);
        put(dot, p.x, p.y);
      } else if (t >= A.ask[1] && t < A.item) {
        const u = eSoft(prog(t, A.ask[1], A.item));
        dot.style.opacity = String(1 - u);
        put(dot, lerp(G.item.x - 8, G.item.x + 10, u), G.item.y + G.item.h / 2);
      } else off(dot);

      /* 2. the order is in the inbox, and the business delivers it */
      itemG.classList.toggle("on", t >= A.item);
      itemG.classList.toggle("res", t >= A.kept);

      /* where the rows are: the pass row and the one it overtakes trade places */
      const moved = t < mid ? 1 : t < A.swap[0] ? 0 : eSoft(prog(t, A.swap[0], A.swap[1]));
      const passY = lerp(restY(G.pass.r), endY(G.pass.r), moved);

      /* the receipts' route ends on the bakery's listing, wherever it is; at the top of the loop
         it glides back down while the rows are faded, rather than jumping when they do */
      const dm = within(t, A.reset) ? 1 - eSoft(prog(t, A.reset[0], A.reset[1])) : moved;
      const doorY = lerp(restY(G.pass.r), endY(G.pass.r), dm) + half;
      if (doorY !== doorAt) {
        doorAt = doorY;
        linkEl.setAttribute("d", linkTo(doorY));
        doorEl.setAttribute("cy", String(doorY));
      }

      /* 3. its inbox signs a receipt */
      const signed = t >= A.seal && t < A.settle[1];
      if (live && crossed(prev, t, A.seal)) flash(slip, "pop", 640);
      slip.classList.toggle("signed", signed);

      /* 4. the customer's agent signs it too: its seal comes along its own line, through the inbox's
         door and down onto the receipt, where the second seal fills in the agent's colour */
      if (live && crossed(prev, t, A.sign[0])) flash(agent, "wake", 640);
      if (within(t, A.sign)) {
        const v = prog(t, A.sign[0], A.sign[1]);
        const p = signPath.getPointAtLength(eSine(v) * LSIGN);
        ink.style.opacity = String(v < 0.12 ? v / 0.12 : 1);
        put(ink, p.x, p.y);
      } else off(ink);
      if (live && crossed(prev, t, A.sign[1])) flash(slip, "copop", 640);
      slip.classList.toggle("cosigned", t >= A.sign[1] && t < A.settle[1]);

      /* 5. and just the receipt, with both seals, travels */
      msgG.classList.toggle("stay", t >= A.road[0] && t < A.road[1] + 0.3);
      if (t < A.slip || t >= A.settle[1]) {
        off(slip);
      } else if (t < A.road[0]) {
        const u = eSoft(prog(t, A.slip, A.slip + 0.25));
        slip.style.opacity = String(u);
        put(slip, birth.x, birth.y, 0.4 + 0.6 * u);
      } else if (t < A.road[1]) {
        const p = roadPath.getPointAtLength(eSine(prog(t, A.road[0], A.road[1])) * LROAD);
        slip.style.opacity = "1";
        put(slip, p.x, p.y);
      } else if (t < A.settle[0]) {
        /* docked on the listing, and carried with it when it moves up */
        slip.style.opacity = "1";
        put(slip, G.dockX, passY + half);
      } else {
        /* and taken into the record, toward the notch it earned */
        const u = eSoft(prog(t, A.settle[0], A.settle[1]));
        slip.style.opacity = String(1 - u);
        put(slip, lerp(G.dockX, notchX, u), passY + half, 1 - 0.4 * u);
      }

      /* 6. the listing's record grows a notch */
      if (live && crossed(prev, t, A.road[1])) flash(pass, "ping", 760);
      if (live && crossed(prev, t, A.notch)) flash(gain, "grow", 720);
      pass.classList.toggle("hit", t >= A.road[1] && t < A.settle[1]);
      const gained = t >= A.notch || t < mid;
      gain.classList.toggle("on", gained);
      gain.classList.toggle("new", gained);

      /* 7. the order follows kept promises */
      dirs.forEach((d, i) => {
        d.setAttribute("transform", `translate(${G.row.x},${lerp(restY(i), endY(i), moved)})`);
      });
      /* the one that moves up passes in front */
      if (dirsG.lastElementChild !== pass) dirsG.appendChild(pass);

      /* The top of the loop: the directory fades down, takes its old places
         and fades back, under the first phrase and while the eye is on the agent. */
      dirsG.style.opacity = within(t, A.reset) ? String(1 - 0.88 * Math.sin(Math.PI * prog(t, A.reset[0], A.reset[1]))) : "";

      /* 8. a coin meets the glass and falls away; the order does not move */
      const [c0, c1, c2] = A.coin;
      if (t >= c0 && t < c1) {
        const v = prog(t, c0, c1);
        coin.style.opacity = String(v < 0.2 ? v / 0.2 : 1);
        put(coin, C.x, lerp(C.from, C.edge - C.r, v * v));
      } else if (t >= c1 && t < c2) {
        const v = prog(t, c1, c2);
        coin.style.opacity = String(v < 0.3 ? 1 : 1 - (v - 0.3) / 0.7);
        put(coin, C.x + 16 * v, C.edge - C.r - 64 * v + 40 * v * v);
      } else off(coin);
      if (live && crossed(prev, t, c1)) flash(ripple, "hit", 820);
    }

    /* ---- the clock ------------------------------------------------------- */
    let clock = A.rest; /* the piece starts from the picture at rest */
    let prevT = A.rest;
    let last = 0;
    let raf = 0;
    let run = false;
    let seen = true;
    const mq = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)");

    function frame(now: number) {
      if (!run) return;
      clock += Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.05); /* clamped: a stall slows the piece, never teleports it */
      last = now;
      const t = clock % A.loop;
      render(t, prevT, true);
      prevT = t;
      raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }
    /* Resume from a settled state: timers that were cut off by a pause must not
       leave a half-faded phrase or a lit halo behind. */
    function settle() {
      for (const t of timers) clearTimeout(t);
      timers.length = 0;
      phrase.textContent = want;
      phrase.classList.add("on");
      sayG.classList.remove("beat");
      agent.classList.remove("wake");
      ripple.classList.remove("hit");
      slip.classList.remove("pop", "copop");
      gain.classList.remove("grow");
      for (const d of dirs) d.classList.remove("ping");
    }
    function sync() {
      if (fig.classList.contains("tf-still")) return;
      const go = seen && !document.hidden;
      if (go === run) return;
      run = go;
      if (run) {
        fig.classList.remove("tf-paused");
        settle();
        last = performance.now();
        raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
      } else {
        cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
        fig.classList.add("tf-paused");
      }
    }

    /* The still is the picture at rest, drawn by this same machine. */
    function still() {
      fig.classList.add("tf-still");
      settle();
      render(A.rest, A.rest, false);
    }

    render(A.rest, A.rest, false);
    if (mq.matches) {
      still();
      return;
    }
    if ("IntersectionObserver" in window) {
      new IntersectionObserver(
        (es) => {
          seen = es[0]?.isIntersecting ?? true;
          sync();
        },
        { threshold: 0.01 },
      ).observe(fig);
    }
    document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", sync);
    /* The preference can be turned on after the page has loaded; both paths end
       in the same frame. */
    mq.addEventListener("change", () => {
      if (!mq.matches || fig.classList.contains("tf-still")) return;
      run = false;
      cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
      still();
    });
    sync();
  }

  /* One figure that throws must not take the page's other figures with it, and
     leaves its own picture at rest standing. */
  function mountAll() {
    for (const f of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".stf")) {
      try {
        mount(f);
      } catch (err) {
        console.warn("trust flow", err);
      }
    }
  }
  mountAll();
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", mountAll);
</script>
